ted both binaries:\n\n- 20 hand-picked cases (overflow edges, `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN`, `2147483648`, `4294967296`, `\"0x10\"`/`\"010\"`, `\"+-3\"`, leading tabs/newlines, empty strings, extra argv entries) — all identical in stdout **and** exit status.\n- 400 randomized pairs across the full `int` range — zero mismatches.\n- Missing-argument cases (`no args`, `one arg`) — both exit 139 with no output.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (checksum verified, clean status).\n\nOne note on tooling noise: rust-analyzer flags `expected !, found ()` at the end of `null_dereference` and a `non_snake_case` hit on a `None` match arm. Both are false positives — `rustc` accepts the file cleanly, since the function ends in `std::process::abort()`, which diverges."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":21004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":693,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f81e978-ae10-4d2c-9ca3-b43acba5cfbe","uuid":"cf08698f-e6c1-428b-928b-52a1a6d85b92","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:13:05.117Z"}
